<!--
  The zones of #13, as OSM has them (relation ids and tags checked 2026-11-07), as squares of 1° along the equator
  with no roads: an origin in each tells its zone by its start country. A square inside another is 0.6° by 0.6°.

    0°–1°E     Kosovo, r2088990: admin_level=2, ISO3166-1:alpha3=XKK                                     RKS
    2°–4°E     Cyprus, r307787, the whole island                                                         CYP
               with Northern Cyprus, r2514541, admin_level=3, inside it at 2.2°–2.8°E                    NX
    4°–5°E     Akrotiri and Dhekelia, r3263728: admin_level=2 without an ISO code                        CYP
    6°–8°E     Moldova, r58974, with Transnistria, r2607033, admin_level=4, inside it at 7.2°–7.8°E      MDA
    9°–11°E    Russia, r60189, and 10°–12°E Ukraine, r60199, overlapping at 10°–11°E                RUS, UKR
               with Crimea, r72639, at 10.2°–10.5°E and Sevastopol, r1574364, at 10.5°–10.8°E,
               both admin_level=4, inside both                                                        CRIMEA
    13°–15°E   Georgia, r28699                                                                           GEO
               with Abkhazia, r1152720, at 13.2°–13.8°E and South Ossetia, r1152717, at 14.2°–14.8°E,
               both admin_level=3                                                ABKHAZIA, SOUTH_OSSETIA
    16°–17°E   the Gaza Strip, r1473938: admin_level=4, in no country                                   GAZA
    18°–20°E   Morocco, r3630439, and 20°–21°E r5441968: admin_level=2 without an ISO code               MAR
               with all of Western Sahara, r2559126: no admin_level, ISO3166-1:alpha3=ESH, over
               19°–21°E                                                                       WESTERN_SAHARA

  The shipped border table closes RKS, UKR and the territories for everyone: no ring from them. Elsewhere, with no
  roads, no_roads.
-->
